# DTF tier manifest: scan-queue-hosted-ahead-of-backfill
#   (artifact-keeper#6032, #6033; fixed for 1.12.1, version floor 1.12.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-files (a stdlib-python upstream the
# oracle fills with npm packages) + limits.scan-one-permit
# (MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_EXTRACTIONS=1). LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts come from the
# backend image's bundled Grype and its seeded DB. The oracle recreates only
# the backend (same postgres, data volume and mock) for each phase with
# fixtures/scan-queue.yml (SCAN_QUEUE_ENABLED=true, the worker on or off), and
# per phase fixtures/worker-concurrency.yml and fixtures/backfill-aging.yml.
#
# THE BUGS
# #6032  With the durable scan queue on, hosted scans (hosted_upload,
#        hosted_image) sat at priority 10, below every fail_open/record_only
#        proxy scan (proxy_file, 50), with no aging: a burst of cold proxy
#        fetches held back every upload and push verdict until the proxy
#        backlog was empty. Since the fix hosted scans are claimed ahead of
#        younger backfill, and a backfill job counts as queued
#        SCAN_QUEUE_BACKFILL_AGING_SECS (default 600) later than it was, so it
#        still goes ahead of hosted scans queued more than the window after it.
# #6033  SCAN_WORKER_CONCURRENCY unset was a fixed 4 whatever
#        MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_EXTRACTIONS said, so a one-permit pod claimed four
#        jobs (three held a claim and showed as `running` while they waited).
#
# HOW THE ORDER IS MADE DETERMINISTIC: every backlog is queued with the worker
# OFF (each first pull through the fail_open Remote is served 200 pending and
# queues one proxy_file job), then the backend is recreated with the worker
# ON and SCAN_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1, so jobs run one at a time in claim order
# and completion timestamps (scan_results.completed_at,
# proxy_scan_results.scanned_at) are the claim order.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX) RED on 1.12.0, GREEN on the fix:
#     #6032 60 proxy_file jobs queued, then a generic upload and an image push
#           into scan_on_upload repositories: both hosted verdicts land within
#           45 s of the worker starting with at most 1 backlog verdict before
#           them (pre-fix: all 60 first), and the backlog then drains.
#     #6032 aging, window 20 s: 3 backfill jobs queued 35 s before a hosted
#           upload, 3 queued right after it. Verdicts land old backfill, then
#           the upload, then the new backfill (pre-fix: the upload last; a
#           "hosted always first" claim: the upload first).
#     #6033 SCAN_WORKER_CONCURRENCY unset, one extraction permit:
#           ak_scan_worker_slots_capacity is 1 and no more than 1 scan_queue
#           row is `running` while a 12-job backlog drains (pre-fix: 4).
#   (CONTROL) on both images: the backlog fully drains with no proxy_file job
#           left; SCAN_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=2 reports capacity 2.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~100 pulls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
COVERS="6032 6033"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files limits.scan-one-permit"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
